>> title: Red-Braised Pork Belly
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: pork, chinese, soy sauce, braise, hong shao rou
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: hong shao rou, hongshao rou, red cooked pork, Shanghai braised pork belly
>> servings: 4
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the caramel at the start is sugar taken dark and it is bitter about ten seconds later, with nowhere to hide it in a pot this small; the ninety-minute braise is forgiving, and the fifteen-minute reduction at the end is standing right there
>> step.1: blanch 5 min
>> step.3: turn in the caramel
>> step.4: braise covered 1 1/2 hr
>> step.5: reduce to a syrupy glaze 15 min

Blanch @skin-on pork belly{2%lb}(900 g; cut in 1 1/2-in cubes), @scallions{2}, @fresh ginger{4%slices}, @water{4%cup}(950 mL) in a #pot{} for ~{5%min}.

Caramelize @rock sugar{2%Tbs}(30 g), @peanut oil{1%Tbs} in a #wok{} until amber.

Turn @&(~2)blanched pork belly{} in @&(~1)caramel{}.

Braise @&(~1)glazed pork{} with @Shaoxing wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @light soy sauce{3%Tbs}, @dark soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @star anise{2}, @cinnamon stick{1}, @water{2%cup}(475 mL) for ~{90%min}.

Reduce @&(~1)braise{} until the sauce is syrupy, ~{15%min}.
